    {
        id types
        title "Port hfst-types (data types, exceptions, symbol defs, string utils)"
        priority 6
        deps (scaffold idiom2)
        log (
            {
                at 2026-06-28T12:12:44.174434Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @decision
                text "Repurposed to Stage 3 (post-idiomatization): the original per-crate breakdown (types/core/openfst/ol/facade/parsers/capi) is now the work of reviewing the monolithic hfst crate and splitting it back into coherent layered crates. Bumped P0/P1/P2 -> P6/P7/P8 and gated `types` on `idiom2` so the decomposition runs after Wave 4 Stage 1 (memory-safety) and Stage 2 (de-C-ism / drop libc). Per nplan_decisions [dec:hfst:idiomatize-staging]."
            }
        )
    }

    {
        id core
        title "Port hfst-core (tokenizer, flag diacritics, HfstBasicTransducer, transition graph, convert)"
        priority 6
        deps (types)
        children (
            {
                id core.util
                title "string-conversions, tokenizer, flag diacritics, epsilon handler, harmonize"
                priority 6
                deps (types)
            }

            {
                id core.basic
                title "transition data/graph + HfstBasicTransducer (the interchange format)"
                priority 6
                deps (core.util)
            }

            {
                id core.convert
                title "ConvertTransducerFormat (HfstBasicTransducer ↔ backend interchange)"
                priority 6
                deps (core.basic)
            }
        )
    }

    {
        id openfst
        title "Reimplement used OpenFST subset (hfst-openfst): VectorFst, semirings, algorithms, SymbolTable, binary I/O"
        priority 6
        deps (types)
        children (
            {
                id openfst.containers
                title "VectorFst, Transition, tropical/log semirings, SymbolTable, state/transition iterators"
                priority 6
                deps (types)
            }

            {
                id openfst.algo
                title "compose/determinize/minimize/shortest-path/push/encode/rm-eps/equivalent + basic ops"
                priority 6
                deps (openfst.containers)
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-07-03T11:40:32.617752Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Weighted-determinize blowup (found 2026-07-03 via lang-sma tokeniser). tropical minimize/determinize (tropical_weight_transducer.rs ~1661/1697) encode with EncodeLabels ONLY when encode_weights=false (the default the pmatch archive minimize uses): the (ilabel,olabel) pair folds into one label so Determinize runs on a weighted ACCEPTOR, but arc weights stay tropical — so it's still WEIGHTED subset construction, which tracks residual weights and cannot merge two paths reaching the same state-set with different residuals. On the sma tokeniser's parallel eps:@PMATCH_ENTRY@ branches this diverges → ~563MB archive. This is NOT a port bug: C++ HFST with the openfst backend produces the identical size (and OpenFst 1.8.4 fstdeterminize explodes the same way). foma does NOT blow up because it determinizes/minimizes UNWEIGHTED automata (boolean subset construction merges freely) — foma is being ported separately. So this is an openfst-family algorithmic property, to be addressed here in the hfst-openfst determinize reimplementation (or by deferring these builds to the foma backend when it lands). Possible levers: EncodeWeightsAndLabels (fold weight into the label → truly unweighted determinize; helps only if weight diversity is low), or skipping the build-time weighted minimize where the OL runtime doesn't require a minimal weighted FST."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-07-03T13:42:41.175234Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Blowup probes (2026-07-03, sma tokeniser-disamb pmscript, all measured with /usr/bin/time -l): (1) C++ HFST 3.17.1 (persistent build at ~/git/necessary/hfst-cpp/dist) produces 538M in 86s/11.2GB peak; Rust produces 538M in 143s/11.3GB — near-byte-identical (one 4-byte length field differs by ~3KB out of 46.7MB in the first def), confirming NOT a port bug. (2) Per-def mass (via the now-fixed `hfst summarize` on the archive): the entire 538M is TOP — 553,027 states / 22,756,707 arcs; the only other def is a trivial urlword RTN. (3) encode_weights=true (EncodeWeightsAndLabels, boolean subset construction) in every minimize: 347M (-35%), 111s (-22%), 9.3GB, and `hfst tokenise -g` output on sample text is IDENTICAL to baseline — a real mitigation but no collapse; the disamb weights are too diverse for label-folding to merge much. (4) Skipping the FINAL pmatch archive minimize entirely (env-gated probe, reverted): still 538M/105s — TOP is already ~22.7M arcs coming out of evaluate(); the inflation is distributed across the per-op optimize()/minimize() chain inside pmatch compilation, not one final determinize. Conclusion: inherent to weighted (tropical) subset construction over this pmscript in the openfst family; levers for this node's reimplementation: (a) offer encode-weights minimize as the pmatch default or a pmatch2fst flag (-35% for free, output-equivalent, diverges from C++ bytes), (b) the foma (unweighted) backend port is the real fix, (c) a smarter weighted minimize here."
                    }
                )
            }

            {
                id openfst.io
                title "OpenFST binary FST read/write + header"
                priority 6
                deps (openfst.containers)
            }
        )
    }

