            {
                id idiom5.symbol-coding
                title "KEYSTONE: de-globalize the symbol coding (NUMBER2SYMBOL_MAP/SYMBOL2NUMBER_MAP/MAX_NUMBER + convert-format NUMBER_TO_STRING/STRING_TO_NUMBER) per the divvunspell pattern — coding owned per-transducer on its alphabet (key_table number->symbol + string_to_symbol), reached via &self/&mut self (NOT a threaded &mut Context param, NOT a shared Rc handle); resolution moves up to graph level; cross-transducer ops harmonize via translator vectors. ~80 sites across ~10 core files. Gated by 151 hfst tests."
                priority 4
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-06-30T01:00:05.355151Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @decision
                        text "Design fixed by operator redirect to ~/git/divvun/divvunspell (their production Rust FST lib = house style). Pattern: TransducerAlphabet is OWNED BY EACH TRANSDUCER, reached via the Transducer trait's alphabet(&self)->&TransducerAlphabet / alphabet_mut(&mut self). It holds key_table: Vec<SmolStr> (number->symbol) + string_to_symbol: HashMap (symbol->number) + identity/unknown/operations. add_symbol(&mut self,&str) interns. Cross-transducer ops harmonize via create_translator_from(&mut self, other)->Vec<SymbolNumber>, remapping the other's numbering into self's and extending self's alphabet. NO global static, NO threaded &mut Context param, NO shared Rc handle. Mapping to the HFST port: HfstBasicTransducer already owns alphabet: HfstAlphabet (a symbol SET); enrich the per-transducer coding so the arc's input_number/output_number resolve against the OWNING graph's coder; move HfstTropicalTransducerTransitionData::get_symbol/get_number (static, ~80 sites: hfst_basic_transducer, both weight transducers, all convert_*, compose_intersect_*, hfst_basic_transition) to instance access through &self; harmonize on binary ops (leverage HFST's existing harmonize machinery). Stage as: K1 extract global coding into an owned SymbolCoder struct (refactor, test-green); K2 thread it onto the transducers as a field; K3 switch resolution to per-transducer + harmonize, delete the globals. 151 hfst tests gate each stage. See memory divvunspell-coding-pattern."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-06-30T01:15:01.041923Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @status
                        text "Todo → Doing (nplan_start)"
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-06-30T02:07:18.652188Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @blocker
                        text "K2/K3 analysis (Explore, high-effort): the global tropical numbering is load-bearing for the algebra, unlike divvunspell's read-only model. Arcs store only u32; binary ops combine numbers across transducers DIRECTLY. Site map: 36 direct static-accessor calls — 17 in HfstBasicTransducer methods (have &self → self.coder), 17 in compose-intersect wrappers (hold a transducer → reachable), 2 in HfstBasicTransition::new_from_basic (class B — no graph, needs coder param); PLUS ~100 transition-data instance-method calls (.get_input_symbol/.get_output_symbol/.set_*/new_symbols) on HfstBasicTransition/HfstTropicalTransducerTransitionData — these have NO owning graph, so their signatures must gain a &SymbolCoder param and ALL ~100 callers ripple. 3 harmonization bottlenecks where per-transducer coders break correctness without an explicit translate/renumber: compose_intersect_lexicon.rs:334 (combines lexicon ilabel + rule olabel), convert_tropical_weight_transducer.rs:138-195 (OpenFst→HFST via get_harmonization_vector), hfst_transducer.rs:4532 (harmonize_ contract). So K3 = one big coherent change: add coder field + populate from each transducer's symbols (a renumber pass, since arcs hold global numbers) + retarget the 36 accessor sites + thread &SymbolCoder through the transition methods to ~100 callers + implement harmonize-renumber at the 3 bottlenecks. The 151 tests (compose/intersect/xerox-rules exercise binary ops) gate it. Highest-risk, largest change in the port; no clean small committable sub-step (field + sig-change + caller-ripple interlock). K1 (encapsulation) is banked."
