                        text "Model switched from config-on-transducer (approach a) to THREADED EngineConfig (approach b), per operator (2026-06-30), after investigation showed the 7 flags are process-global ENGINE POLICY, not per-transducer attributes: (1) toggled by XFST `set` commands / CLI flags = session modes with no transducer to attach to at the moment they run; (2) encode_weights is read 3 levels into the tropical backend (tropical_weight_transducer.rs:1757/1791/2228) on a raw StdVectorFst with no HfstTransducer in scope (would need threading regardless); (3) matches the idiom5 charter's own words \"thread it through an explicit context\". Design: an owned EngineConfig {can_minimize, minimize_even_if_already_minimal, unknown_symbols_in_use, flag_is_epsilon_in_composition, encode_weights, minimization_algorithm, harmonize_smaller} with Default = today's C++ defaults. Public ops keep their signature as thin wrappers using EngineConfig::default() (so the 152 tests stay byte-identical, no global); a *_with_config variant threads a configured one; XFST/CLI own an EngineConfig and call the configured variants, threading it into internal minimize/compose calls. Subsumes the 2 backend hopcroft atomics (openfst_tropical/log_use_hopcroft): minimization_algorithm threads as use_hopcroft: bool into the backend minimize, deleting those too. xerox_composition still deferred (pmatch-toggled) to keep edits disjoint from idiom5.scratch."
                    }

