                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @note
                text "pmatch de-RefCell design (validated 2026-07-06): NOT a full arena. Analysis showed nodes mutate ONLY cache + my_timer during evaluate (set_left/set_right are dead code; children immutable post-construction), and only named-definition nodes cache (should_use_cache = get_name()!=\"\" && call_stack_len()==0) which persist in definitions_table for the whole compile. So: ObjRef/PairRef Rc<RefCell<dyn>> -> Rc<dyn> (immutable shared, DAG sharing kept); cache moves to ctx side-table HashMap<usize,HfstTransducer> keyed by node address (std::ptr::from_ref(self) as *const () as usize — SAFE cast, staleness-free since cacheable nodes never freed mid-compile); my_timer -> returned local from start_timing; all 41 recursive trait methods &mut self -> &self; recursion .borrow_mut().m() -> .m(). Immutable &self re-entry structurally kills the self-referential-definition double-borrow panic. Far less churn than arena (no NodeId, no parser threading, no take/replace). Byte-identity via same eval order + same cache semantics. Oracle: 538MB tokeniser + errmodel + 152 tests."
                after_done true
            }
        )
    }

